,"/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids October to November and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years. In 2025, July to August ran 37% of normal and November to December 35% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, Jan-Feb came in at 49% and Feb-Mar at 46% on the middle of the grids. Grid 18766 had its driest year in 1963 at 64% of normal.</p>"}
